  "interpretation": "Mutation timing intervention usually generated the intended finite-threshold phenotypic ordering. The independent16 preregistered persistence interaction FAILED and the balanced exploratory pooled persistence interaction was zero. Historical trait and immediate-payoff contrasts can therefore change without a stable improvement in survival under the declared stress.",
  "claim_boundary": [
    "Observed threshold order is not a direct intervention on phenotype",
    "One-sided crossing does not establish the unobserved trait never experienced selection",
    "Prehistory arms within each visitor history and nested repeats are not independent ecological histories",
    "The viability audit is post-outcome explanatory, not a new confirmatory gate",
    "A mismatch between immediate viability and final occupancy cannot be interpreted as viability causally unrelated to persistence, given finite demographic sampling",
    "All natural-island interpretations remain hypotheses"
